{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-20 05:48:57 UTC] [Agent: ArchitectAgent] [Project: agent_param_audit] Starting architecture design for agent parameter standardization. Reviewed research document which identifies 14 tools needing changes across 3 categories: make agent REQUIRED (4 tools), add agent as REQUIRED (9 tools), rename agent_id to agent (1 tool). Diagnostic tools (health_check, doctor) excluded from scope. | approach=verify_existing_docs_then_design; reasoning={\"how\": \"Architecture-first approach: verify existing architecture docs, examine enforcement in server.py, design phased implementation with backward compatibility strategy\", \"what\": \"14 tools need parameter changes - 4 Optional\\u2192Required, 9 missing entirely, 1 rename agent_id\\u2192agent. Constraint: maintain backward compatibility where possible\", \"why\": \"Need to standardize agent parameter across all MCP tools for consistent session tracking and audit trails\"}; research_doc=RESEARCH_AGENT_PARAM_AUDIT_20260120.md; task=agent_param_standardization; tools_affected=14; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/agent_param_audit/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-20T05:48:57.029848+00:00_ad1e6eb4", "timestamp": "2026-01-20T05:48:57.029910+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-20T05:48:57.029848+00:00_ad1e6eb4", "timestamp": "2026-01-20T05:48:57.041371+00:00"}
{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-20 05:49:12 UTC] [Agent: ArchitectAgent] [Project: agent_param_audit] Verified existing architecture documents exist but are generic templates - need complete replacement for agent parameter standardization project. Found server.py line 355: hard failure enforcement 'agent parameter is required for all tool calls'. This confirms REQUIRED status is the target state. | finding=hard_fail_line_355; reasoning={\"how\": \"Read server.py around line 355 to understand the enforcement logic and exceptions\", \"what\": \"Found ValueError raise if agent parameter missing - this is the enforcement that breaks tools without agent param\", \"why\": \"Need to understand enforcement mechanism before designing parameter additions\"}; verification=server_enforcement; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/agent_param_audit/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-20T05:49:12.431565+00:00_b029b193", "timestamp": "2026-01-20T05:49:12.431606+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-20T05:49:12.431565+00:00_b029b193", "timestamp": "2026-01-20T05:49:12.442511+00:00"}
{"op": "append", "content": "[\u26a0\ufe0f] [2026-01-20 05:49:22 UTC] [Agent: ArchitectAgent] [Project: agent_param_audit] Critical finding: server.py has unconditional agent parameter enforcement at line 355 with NO exceptions. This means health_check and scribe_doctor (which have zero parameters) will also fail unless we add agent parameter to them OR create an exception list in server.py. Design decision required. | affected_tools=[\"health_check\", \"scribe_doctor\"]; issue=diagnostic_tools_will_fail; reasoning={\"how\": \"Need to decide which approach maintains better system consistency and usability\", \"what\": \"Two approaches: (1) Add agent parameter to diagnostics, (2) Create exception list in server.py for diagnostic tools\", \"why\": \"Diagnostic tools traditionally have no parameters, but server enforcement requires agent parameter universally\"}; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/agent_param_audit/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-20T05:49:22.165752+00:00_8753f958", "timestamp": "2026-01-20T05:49:22.165789+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-20T05:49:22.165752+00:00_8753f958", "timestamp": "2026-01-20T05:49:22.175905+00:00"}
{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-20 05:49:50 UTC] [Agent: ArchitectAgent] [Project: agent_param_audit] Analyzed existing tool signatures. Pattern identified: set_project has agent as 2nd parameter (after name), append_entry has agent as 4th parameter (after message/status/emoji). Design decision: agent should be positioned early but after primary identifier (name, path, action). This maintains consistency while keeping tool-specific primary parameters first. | analysis=parameter_positioning; examples={\"append_entry\": \"message, status, emoji, agent, ...\", \"proposed_manage_docs\": \"action, agent, doc_category, ...\", \"set_project\": \"name, agent, ...\"}; pattern=agent_after_primary_id; reasoning={\"how\": \"Determined agent should come early in signature after primary identifier parameter to maintain discoverability while not disrupting existing parameter semantics\", \"what\": \"Analyzed set_project (REQUIRED agent), append_entry (OPTIONAL agent), manage_docs (missing agent) to understand positioning patterns\", \"why\": \"Need consistent parameter positioning across all tools for predictable API\"}; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/agent_param_audit/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-20T05:49:50.290196+00:00_c53d709d", "timestamp": "2026-01-20T05:49:50.290242+00:00"}
