{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-20 05:51:06 UTC] [Agent: ArchitectAgent] [Project: agent_param_audit] Completed Problem Statement and Requirements sections. Key architectural decision identified: diagnostic tools (health_check, scribe_doctor) currently have zero parameters. Two options: (1) Add agent param to them for consistency, (2) Create exception list in server.py. Leaning toward Option 1 for system-wide consistency - all tools should have agent tracking. | decision_point=diagnostic_tools; options=[\"add_agent_param\", \"server_exception_list\"]; reasoning={\"how\": \"Analysis shows diagnostic tools can accept agent param without semantic harm - they're system utilities that should still track which agent invoked them for audit purposes\", \"what\": \"Option 1 (add param) provides system-wide consistency. Option 2 (exception list) adds complexity to server.py and creates special cases\", \"why\": \"Need to decide how to handle parameterless diagnostic tools under universal agent enforcement\"}; recommendation=add_agent_param; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/agent_param_audit/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-20T05:51:06.732744+00:00_ad57b57a", "timestamp": "2026-01-20T05:51:06.732810+00:00"}
